#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:706
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reprocess Failed Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:711
msgid ""
"When Zammad fetches an email it cannot parse (e.g. due to a parser bug or a "
"malformed message), it will store the email in the database and warn in the "
"monitoring section about it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:715
msgid ""
"In case of a malformed message (e.g. an invalid email address in one of the "
"header fields), you may need to manually edit the email before Zammad can "
"process it. To do so, follow the steps below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:716
#, no-wrap
msgid "Export all Failed Emails to a Local Folder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:717
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:export_all`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:723
msgid ""
"You can find the location of the exported email in the output of your "
"console.  Every time you perform an export of failed (unprocessable) emails, "
"it creates one folder containing all failed emails at the time of execution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:724
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edit the Email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:728
msgid ""
"The email has been exported in the step above. Now you can have a look at it "
"and try to repair it. Make sure to leave the file name untouched, as the "
"import will otherwise fail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:729
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import and Reprocess Locally Modified Email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:732
msgid "After editing the email, run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:733
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:import path/to/your/email.eml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:741
msgid ""
"This will apply your changes from the file to the database. You can also "
"pass the entire folder as argument, so all `.eml` files in it will we "
"imported and reprocessed. If the reprocessing of the email was successful, "
"the file(s) will be deleted, and the empty folder removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:742
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Make sure to run these commands only from the main Zammad folder\n"
"`/opt/zammad`. There may be problems if you try to run it from within\n"
"the generated subfolder.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:748
#, no-wrap
msgid "Delete Unwanted Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:752
msgid ""
"In case of unwanted emails such as spam, you can delete them from the "
"database after exporting them with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:752
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:delete path/to/your/email.eml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:759
msgid ""
"If you pass the export folder as argument instead, all contained emails will "
"be removed from the database, their files deleted and finally the empty "
"folder removed."
msgstr ""

