#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:61
msgid ""
"There are several events in terms of an ongoing call. These actions always "
"come from your PBX system and may be:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:65
msgid "\"newCall\" event (initiation of a call)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:65
msgid "\"hangup\" event (call ending)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:65
msgid "\"answer\" event (aka picking up the phone)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:70
msgid ""
"In some situations Zammad may provide a return on your PBX calls (e.g. a "
"reject) if you blocked a specific caller. Zammad will never initiate "
"specific actions with your PBX. Zammad is a passive component in all "
"described cases."
msgstr ""

